Description: Leave the sign-in routes to the platform; serve a shim instead of rewriting the app
 The platform now routes the sign-in sidecar itself: /sso/login and /sso/acs
 of the app's host reach the sidecar at the platform's edge, and a page load of
 /sign-in or /sign-up is redirected there. This nginx is therefore no longer in
 the path of a sign-in, and three things 0005 and 0006 added for it go:
 .
  - the two locations that proxied /api/v1/authn/saml/{login,acs} to the
    sidecar, and with them the lookup of the sidecar's address at start, which
    ended the container when the sidecar's Service was not there yet;
  - the redirect of every page to the sign-in unless a cookie named ap_token
    was present, and the cookie set from a ?token= query parameter. The session
    is not in a cookie any more: the sidecar writes it where Activepieces' page
    keeps it, in localStorage, and no cookie carries the token;
  - the rewrite of the shipped index.html at container start (the L5 residue
    0006 recorded). nginx has ngx_http_sub_module in this image, so the one
    script the page needs is served as a file and referenced by a sub_filter,
    as 0006's own exit criterion asked.
 .
 What stays is that script (files/sign-in.js). Activepieces' page moves to its
 own sign-in form by itself when it has no token or finds it run out, without a
 request the edge could redirect, and nobody has a password to type there. The
 script sends the browser to /sso/login instead.
 .
 gentian.sso.host and gentian.startup.injectSessionScript are removed with what
 read them. Guarded by gentian.enabled as before: unset, output is unchanged.
Author: Gentian Platform <platform@gentian.org>
Origin: other, https://github.com/gentian-org/gentian-apps
Forwarded: not-needed
Reason: Gentian platform integration glue, as 0005 and 0006; upstream has no
 reason to carry it.
Applied-Upstream: no
